{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"metadata":{"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Working with TfNotice","modules":[{"name":"OpenUSD"}]},"abstract":[{"text":"Learn how to use the TfNotice notification subsystem in Swift","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftusd\/workingwithtfnotice"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]},{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftusd\/workingwithtfnotice"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"occ"}]}],"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OpenUSD includes a notification subsystem based on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pxr::TfNotice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pxr::TfNotice::Register"},{"type":"text","text":" for use in C++. SwiftUsd exposes this system to Swift with minor modifications."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Like in C++, TfNotice registration in Swift comes in three main forms:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUsd\/documentation\/OpenUSD\/C++\/pxr\/TfNotice\/Register(_:_:)-28red","isActive":true,"type":"reference","overridingTitle":"pxr.TfNotice.Register(_:_:)","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"code":"pxr.TfNotice.Register(_:_:)","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"text":" to register for a particular notice type, regardless of sender","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pxr.TfNotice.Register(_:_:_:)"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUsd\/documentation\/OpenUSD\/C++\/pxr\/TfNotice\/Register(_:_:_:)-22ec6","overridingTitle":"pxr.TfNotice.Register(_:_:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" to register for a particular notice type from a specific sender, without retrieving the sender in the notificat